    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> was raised from a principality to a kingdom in 1882 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> I of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obrenovic-dynasty">House of Obrenović</a>.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-serbia">May Coup</a> of 1903 killed King Alexander I and Queen Draga, brought Peter I of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karadordevic-dynasty">Karađorđević dynasty</a> to the throne and turned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</li><li>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a> of 1912–1913 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>'s population rose from 2.9 million to 4.5 million and its territory by 81%, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sandzak">Sandžak</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar-macedonia">Vardar Macedonia</a> annexed.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>By the beginning of the 1880s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and Montenegro were the only European nations without railroads; one conservative deputy warned that building them would make Serbia suffer the fate of the Indians after the discovery of America.</p></aside>
    </section>

